Title: B-cell Hybrid Immune Variant Engine
Description: bHIVE implements an artificial immune network (AI-Net) for
        clustering and classification of high-dimensional data such as
        mass cytometry and single-cell profiles. A population of
        prototypes, called antibodies, evolves by clonal selection,
        somatic hypermutation and network suppression, and the learned
        prototypes summarize cell populations in the original marker
        units. The same fitted model clusters a dataset and labels new
        cells. bHIVE accepts SummarizedExperiment and
        SingleCellExperiment objects and integrates with bluster
        through bHIVEParam. A C++ backend computes affinities,
        mutations and suppression, and optional R6 modules add
        mechanisms such as germinal center selection,
        microenvironment-dependent mutation and isotype switching. The
        package also provides multilayer clustering, grid search and
        caret model wrappers.
