Title: Scalable Two-Tier Causal Discovery for Multi-Omic Data
Description: Causal ASCEND (Ancestral Scalable Causal discovEry via
        iNherited Descent) infers ancestral (cause-before-effect)
        relations among downstream molecular variables, such as gene
        expression, when a layer of upstream variables, such as
        genotypes or methylation sites, is known to precede them. Each
        conditional independence test conditions only on a small,
        iteratively refined set of nearest ancestors instead of the
        whole upstream layer, so the number of tests grows polynomially
        with the number of variables. The package accepts matrices,
        SummarizedExperiment objects or a MultiAssayExperiment, and
        returns the ancestral relations with the rule and evidence
        behind each one.
