Title: Homologous Recombination Detection in Nuclear Families
Description: This package implements a nuclear family-based algorithm
        to detect homologous recombination. Using genotypes in PLINK
        binary format, recombination events are inferred from changes
        in the inheritance state of informative SNPs between siblings.
        Closely spaced crossovers that are unlikely to represent true
        recombination can be filtered out using genetic maps or a
        SNP-count filter. Additional functions are supplied to detect
        runs of homozygosity and to phase haplotypes at informative
        SNPs and intervals that are inferred identical-by-descent.
        Recombination intervals and runs of homozygosity are returned
        as `GRanges` objects, and phased genotypes are returned as a
        `VariantAnnotation` `VCF` object, for use with other
        Bioconductor packages and genome browsers.
