Title: Isoform-Level Protein Interaction Network Analysis
Description: Compares predicted protein-interaction neighbourhoods of
        transcript isoforms. The user supplies isoform seeds labelled
        "up" or "down", for example the isoforms that gain or lose
        usage in a differential transcript usage analysis. Each seed
        set is expanded in a bundled isoform-resolved predicted
        interaction network, or in a user-supplied igraph network, and
        the resulting neighbourhoods are compared per gene and
        summarised across genes. The package also provides
        connected-component analysis, network diagnostics, plots, and
        over-representation and gene set enrichment analysis of
        neighbourhood statistics. Protein-identical transcripts are
        resolved to shared representatives, and nonsense-mediated and
        non-stop decay transcripts, annotated from Ensembl through
        AnnotationHub, are excluded by default. Results are S4Vectors
        DataFrames, and gene sets can be GSEABase collections such as
        those of the msigdb package. Statistical testing of isoform
        usage remains upstream of the package.
biocViews: Software, Network, GraphAndNetwork, NetworkEnrichment,
        GeneSetEnrichment, AlternativeSplicing, DifferentialSplicing,
        Transcriptomics, SystemsBiology, Visualization
