Title: Tools for LC-MSn-Based Metabolomics: Precursor Ion Purity
        Assessment, Fragmentation Data and Spectral Tree Processing,
        and Spectral Matching
Description: Provides tools for precursor ion purity assessment,
        processing fragmentation data and spectral trees, and spectral
        matching in LC-MSn-based metabolomics. Precursor ion purity
        estimates the contribution of a selected precursor to the
        signal within its isolation window, using neighbouring MS1
        measurements for MS2 and linked parent fragmentation spectra
        for higher MSn levels. Fragmentation spectra can be associated
        with chromatographic features, filtered and averaged using
        acquisition-aware settings. Mass Spectral Trees link successive
        fragmentation spectra, while Precursor-Fragment Trees connect
        individual precursor and product peaks. Spectral matching
        compares measured or consensus spectra with experimental
        spectra and reference libraries, accounting for MS level,
        precursor relationships and acquisition conditions. The
        optional BLINK method computes approximate cosine similarity as
        described by Harwood et al. (2023)
        <doi:10.1038/s41598-023-40496-9>. Integration with 'Spectra'
        and 'xcms' connects spectrum handling and chromatographic
        feature information. Parquet datasets link raw measurements,
        processed spectra and reference libraries, retaining feature
        associations, processing settings and measurement provenance.
        Reusable parameter objects and recorded processing history
        support reproducible analysis and reopening of processed
        results. Spectrum selection, linked visualisation, library
        import and export, and reporting of feature information and
        spectral matches support downstream interpretation and data
        exchange.
