Title: Missing Value-Aware Differential Abundance Analysis of DIA
        Proteomics Data
Description: Provides an end-to-end workflow for differential abundance
        analysis of protein quantification data, with particular
        attention to missing values in data-independent acquisition
        (DIA) proteomics. Quantification reports exported from
        Spectronaut, DIA-NN and Proteome Discoverer for TMT and
        label-free experiments (DDA/DIA) are converted into a common
        data structure, normalised, optionally batch-corrected, imputed
        and analysed using limma or limpa. The package includes
        individual and two-stage imputation strategies that treat
        values assumed to be missing at random and missing not at
        random separately. Data-driven functions evaluate and rank
        normalisation and imputation workflows using simulated
        missingness or spike-in datasets with known ground truth,
        allowing method selection to be justified for each dataset.
        Results can be explored through interactive Highcharts
        visualisations, static ggplot2 and ComplexHeatmap figures, and
        sortable tables.
