Title: Test Changes in the Co-Localisation of Cell Types Between Groups
        of Patients
Description: spicyR tests whether the spatial co-localisation of pairs
        of cell types differs between groups of patients, or is
        associated with patient outcome, in cell-resolution spatial
        omics data (imaging mass cytometry, CODEX, MIBI, Xenium, CosMx
        and others). Its default method, spicyR Cell, counts the cells
        of one type within a radius of each cell of another and
        compares the count with its exact expectation under random
        labelling of the observed cells. Images are combined within
        patients by a frailty generalised estimating equation, and
        differences are tested with a small-sample cluster-robust (CR2)
        variance with patients as the units. Covariates, several
        conditions, several radii and survival outcomes are supported,
        and the original image-level test is kept as an option. The
        computations run in a C++ core shared with the Python package
        spicyr.
