Title: Taxon Set Enrichment Analysis
Description: TaxSEA makes metagenomic data easier to interpret. Rather
        than reading species one at a time, it tests whether a-priori
        defined sets of taxa shift together, drawing on public
        databases (BugSigDB, MiMeDB, GutMGene, mBodyMap, BacDive and
        GMRepoV2) and on sets collated from the literature. Two
        approaches are provided. TaxSEA takes taxon names or NCBI IDs
        with a rank per taxon, such as a fold change or correlation
        coefficient, and tests each set with a Kolmogorov-Smirnov test.
        ssTaxSEA scores every set in a single sample as the mean
        centered log-ratio of its members, giving a per-sample value to
        use in any downstream model. Both work with any taxonomic
        profiling technology, including 16S rRNA gene sequencing,
        shotgun metagenomics and metatranscriptomics.
