Title: Weighted Omics View Embedding via Nystrom for Incomplete
        Multi-Omics Data
Description: Supervised multi-omics integration for block-missing
        ("ragged") data, where some subjects lack one or more whole
        omics modalities (assay blocks) rather than scattered
        individual values. WOVEN fits a shared latent space with SUMCOR
        (sum of correlations) multi-set canonical correlation analysis,
        a criterion that maximizes the summed pairwise correlation
        between modalities' latent scores, using only the anchor
        subjects observed in every modality; class labels enter through
        a label-augmented cross-covariance, and per-modality graph
        Laplacians regularize the fit. Every other subject is then
        scored from the modalities it has by a Nystrom extension, a way
        to place new points in an already fitted embedding (for WOVEN's
        linear embedding, multiplying the observed features by the
        learned projection matrices), so no missing block is imputed.
        The effective sample size (ESS) retention, the fraction of
        subjects a method can score, is therefore the fraction with at
        least one observed modality, rather than the complete-case
        fraction. woven_tune() chooses the regularization settings by
        cross-validated balanced error rate, and the fitted model is
        summarized by plots and a table of the top features per
        modality.
biocViews: Software, StatisticalMethod, DimensionReduction,
        Classification, Clustering, GeneExpression, Transcriptomics,
        Proteomics, Metabolomics
